Careful with normalization rules: accepted: `+375 29 123-45-67` (375 + 9 digits), `375291234567`, `80 29 1234567` (80 + 029... wait 80 29 1234567 = 80 + 29 + 7 = 809? "80" prefix national format: 80 29 123-45-67 → digits `80291234567` (11 digits). Convert: drop leading `8`? No: Belarusian national format for mobile: 8 029 XXX-XX-XX? Actually Belarus: international +375, national trunk prefix `8` then area code `0`? Wait: Belarus mobile numbers: +375 29 XXX-XX-XX; national dialing: 8 029 XXX XX XX (8 + 0 + 29...). Hmm the spec says: "Принимаются форматы: `+375 29 123-45-67`, `375291234567`, `80 29 1234567`, `(029) 1234567`". So "80 29 1234567" → digits `80291234567`. Normalize: strip leading "80" → "291234567" (9 digits) then prefix +375 → +375291234567. And "(029) 1234567" → digits `0291234567` (10 digits) → strip leading "0" → `291234567` → +375. City numbers 17: `(017) 1234567` → `0171234567` → strip 0 → `171234567` → +375171234567. 

Algorithm:
```
let d = digitsOnly(input)
if d starts with '375' → keep
else if d starts with '80' → d = d.slice(2)   // 80 29...
