Task 8 review: 1 Important — open menu + resize across 1024px leaves body scroll locked on desktop with no visible close control. Real bug, plan-mandated code. Fix: close on viewport change via matchMedia listener, or gate the lock on panel visibility.

Ruling: fix. It's a real UX bug (scroll lock stuck); small fix. This deviation from brief-verbatim is sanctioned by me. Options:
(a) matchMedia("(min-width: 1024px)") change → setIsOpen(false).
(b) Gate body lock: `if (isOpen && window.matchMedia("(max-width: 1023px)").matches)` set overflow hidden — but on resize while open, the menu remains "open" state with hidden panel; new burger click toggles closed... The panel is lg:hidden so not visible; user can click burger again (burger visible on mobile only... at ≥1024 burger is hidden). So (a) is cleaner: auto-close when crossing to desktop.

Implementation sketch for implementer:
```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  if (!isOpen) return;
  const media = window.matchMedia("(min-width: 1024px)");
  const close = () => { if (media.matches) setIsOpen(false); };
  media.addEventListener("change", close);
  return () => media.removeEventListener("change", close);
}, [isOpen]);
```
Wait — also if the menu is open and resized back... it's already closed. Also should the effect close immediately if already desktop when opening? Burger is hidden on desktop so it can't open there. Fine.

Alternatively simpler: in the lock effect, add resize listener:
Actually cleanest single effect: when isOpen, listen to matchMedia change and close. Implementer can choose; I'll specify the matchMedia approach.

No test infra for this (no unit tests by design) — verification: lint/typecheck/build + a quick manual note. Since no tests, the fix is small; the re-review verifies the diff.

Fix round 1 → resume implementer ses_ebc96a3a7ffetEAK2KZvW8ymoe with instructions + commit message. The fix is JS behavior; can't easily test in jsdom? Actually they could add a vitest test for MobileMenu... The plan had no unit tests for layout by design. The re-review will just inspect the diff. Per SDD, fix report must include covering tests command run and output — for a no-test task, covering evidence = lint/typecheck/build. That's acceptable ("re-run the tests covering the amended code" — here none exist; the implementer should at least run build/typecheck). The template says confirm fix report contains covering tests, command run, output — if no tests exist, build+typecheck output. Fine.

Also mention minor top-[120px] — defer to Task 13 polish (implementer already flagged; Task 13 does visual checks). Ledger deferred.

Dispatch fix.

